# HATC SEO & Analytics

Build SEO in from the start, not as an afterthought.

## Metadata

- Use the Next.js Metadata API per page (title, description, canonical, OpenGraph, Twitter).
- Localise metadata via next-intl; every page provides all three locales.
- Emit `hreflang` alternates for `zh-Hant` (default), `zh-Hans`, `en`, plus `x-default`.
- **`metadata.*.description` is governed by the same fact red lines as page copy**
  (第五十五輪). It is the first sentence the public sees in search results and is the
  easiest thing to forget after a redesign, so when you touch a page, re-read its
  description:
  - When it names products it must list **all three approved CFDs** — gold, silver and
    the RMB kilobar (`HATC_FACTS.md` → "CFD business") — never just two of them.
  - Keep a「示意」/ "illustrative" caveat **only while that page really does show sample
    content**. `/platforms` carried「平台介面為示意」long after 第五十一／五十二輪 replaced
    the mockups with real terminal screenshots, and `metadata.funding` carried
    「出金渠道與時間為示意數據」until 第六十九輪 published the owner's real channels.
    **The only remaining honest uses are the two placeholder images**
    (`home.mt5.screenshotAlt` = the Figma AI render on the homepage,
    `trading.hero.imageAlt` = the Figma tablet placeholder) **and the market-data
    degradation labels** (`home.heroV2.sampleData`, `home.goldServices.chartSample`,
    which only render when live quotes are unavailable). Nothing else on the site may
    say「示意」— audit with a key-path sweep of `src/messages/*`, not a code grep,
    because most hits live in i18n strings.

## Share cards & app icons (第六十六輪, 2026-10-14)

- **Every page must advertise an image.** The brand card is `SHARE_CARD` in
  `src/lib/seo.ts` (`public/brand/share-card.jpg`, 1200×630), applied in the locale
  layout to both `openGraph.images` and `twitter.images`.
- 🚩 **A page that declares `openGraph` replaces the parent's whole `openGraph`
  object — images included.** This is not a deep merge, and it is silent: declaring
  `openGraph: {title, description, type}` in `/announcements/[slug]` left the page
  with a Twitter image (inherited) and **no `og:image` at all**, i.e. no thumbnail on
  WhatsApp or Facebook while X looked fine. So:
  - when a page sets `openGraph`, give it `images` too (own cover, else `SHARE_CARD`);
  - when its image differs from the layout's, set `twitter.images` as well, or the
    two networks will advertise different pictures (that is what `/academy/[slug]`
    did for months);
  - for the same reason the share card is a plain `public/` asset rather than an
    `opengraph-image.jpg` route file — a file-convention image attaches to one
    segment and vanishes from any descendant that declares `openGraph`.
- **Do not set `og:url` in the layout.** A layout cannot know the current path, so it
  can only name the locale root, and scrapers treat `og:url` as the canonical URL of
  what was shared — every subpage would be reported as the homepage. Omitted, they
  use the fetched URL, which is right. Only set it where the page knows its own path
  (`/academy/[slug]`, `/announcements/[slug]`).
- **Keep uploaded media crawlable.** Article covers are served from
  `/api/media/file/…` and are the `og:image` of every academy article, and the
  Facebook/WhatsApp scrapers honour `robots.txt` — hence `Allow: /api/media/`
  alongside `Disallow: /api` in `src/app/robots.ts`. Do not collapse that back.
- **Card copy is governed by the fact red lines.** It currently carries only the legal
  name and `home.heroV2.badge`（香港黃金交易所 AA類行員 008號）. No trading conditions,
  client counts or award claims.
- **Icons**: `src/app/{favicon.ico,icon.png,apple-icon.png}`, regenerated together with
  the card by `node scripts/generate-brand-images.mjs` from the real wordmark. The mark
  is the "A" glyph plus the green triangle, lifted out of `public/brand/hatc-logo.png`
  by connected-component labelling — the full 3.4:1 wordmark is an unreadable smudge at
  16px, and a rectangular crop cannot avoid the neighbouring "T" crossbar. `icon.png`
  is rounded; `apple-icon.png` is full-bleed because iOS applies its own mask.
- The card's URL is absolute via `metadataBase`, so **a preview host built with
  `prd` settings advertises an image on `www.hatcmarket.com`** — one more reason the
  preview host must use `build:stg` (DEPLOYMENT §2.0a).
- WhatsApp and Telegram cache previews per URL for a long time; expect to append a
  query string when re-checking after a deploy. Keep the card well under ~300 KB
  (currently ~61 KB as JPEG; the same design as PNG was 350 KB and some clients skip
  images that large).

## Webview twins under `/embed` (第七十輪, 2026-10-14; `faq` added 第七十二輪)

`/<locale>/embed/{announcements,announcements/[slug],disclaimer,privacy,faq}` are chrome-less
copies of public pages, rendered for the HATC app / h5 webview. They are duplicates by
design, so they carry a very specific SEO treatment — do not "complete" it:

- `robots: {index: false, follow: false}` is set once in
  `src/app/(embed)/[locale]/embed/layout.tsx` and inherited by every embed page (a page
  that declares its own `robots` would drop it — only `title`/`description` are overridden).
- **No canonical and no `hreflang`, deliberately.** Pointing a canonical at the public
  twin while the page says `noindex` is a contradictory pair of signals and risks the
  noindex being attributed to the canonical target — i.e. deindexing the real page.
- **Not in `sitemap.ts`** (there is a note in that file) and nothing on the site links to
  them, so they are effectively undiscoverable.
- **`robots.txt` stays permissive for `/embed`.** A `Disallow` would stop crawlers from
  ever reading the `noindex`, which is the only signal actually doing the work here.

## Crawlability & structure

- Provide `sitemap.xml` (all locales) and `robots.txt`.
- 🚩 **CMS detail pages are enumerated per locale (第七十一輪).** `src/app/sitemap.ts`
  asks `getAnnouncementSlugsByLocale()` / `getAcademyArticleSlugsByLocale()` which
  locales can actually render each slug, because a document with no title in a locale
  is dropped by its reader and that locale's URL 404s. The previous version derived
  one slug list from the default locale, so seven announcements typed only in
  Simplified Chinese were missing from the sitemap **in every locale** — including the
  Simplified site where they rendered fine. Keep `alternates.languages` limited to the
  locales in the entry; do not "simplify" it back to `routing.locales`.
- `sitemap.ts` is a prerendered route with **no cache tag of its own**, so any reader
  it enumerates must call `revalidateSitemap()` (see `revalidateContent.ts`).
- **Only production may be indexable (第六十二輪).** `siteIndexable` in `src/lib/seo.ts`
  reads `SITE_INDEXABLE`; `false` (set in `config/env/local.env` and `uat.env`) turns
  `robots.txt` into `Disallow: /` **and** emits `noindex, nofollow` on every page.
  Both layers are needed — `robots.txt` only blocks crawling, not indexing of a URL
  someone links to. It is build-time, so a UAT build must set it before `next build`.
  - 🚩 **A `.env.local` on the deployment host silently wins over `config/env/prd.env`
    (第六十三輪).** `.env.local` is loaded by Next even when `NODE_ENV=production`, and
    `scripts/with-env.mjs` deliberately leaves any key it declares alone — so
    `npm run build:prd` does **not** override it. The dev team's committed `.env.local`
    carried `SITE_INDEXABLE=false` + `NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=http://localhost:3000`,
    which would have made the production site emit localhost canonicals and a
    site-wide noindex **with no error and a perfectly normal-looking page**. Production
    hosts must not have a `.env.local`; verification curls are in DEPLOYMENT §2.4.
- **Production host = `https://www.hatcmarket.com`** (owner 2026-10-13, recorded in
  `HATC_FACTS.md`). The relationship between it and the older `www.hatchk.com` is
  **not yet clarified by the owner** — do not add a redirect, a cross-canonical or a
  page that lists both domains.
- `siteUrl` falls back to `http://localhost:3000`. Read it with `||`, never `??`:
  an empty `NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=` used to pass through as `''` and break every
  prerender with `ERR_INVALID_URL` from `new URL(siteUrl)`.
- Semantic HTML: one `<h1>` per page, correct heading order, `<nav>/<main>/<footer>`,
  descriptive `alt` text, meaningful link text.
- Add JSON-LD structured data (e.g. `Organization`) sourced from `docs/HATC_FACTS.md`.
  `OrganizationJsonLd` carries `logo` (the wordmark, not the square app icon — search
  engines want the logo itself, not a logo on a tile).
- Set `<html lang>` to the active locale.

## Analytics / tracking

- Tracking is built in from launch, but IDs/keys are configurable (env or CMS),
  never hard-coded.
- Load tags via `next/script` with appropriate strategy; do not block rendering.
- Respect privacy/consent; keep tracking easy to disable per environment.
